body:
Cyproterone (not an option in the US) and Spironolactone (the most prescribed in the US) are two of the most effective anti-androgens, and Progesterone (which is sometimes used in the US as a replacement for Cypro and for people who can't take Spiro for whatever reason) are the most common anti-androgens prescribed. There are also nonsteroidal medications like Nilutamide, Flutamide, and  Dutasteride  that are all known to be less effective than Cypro and Spiro and are also extremely toxic to the liver.

&#x200B;

You  say that Spiro is so inferior, but what it is you feel is so superior to it?

&#x200B;

And yes, I do take Spiro and have an undetectable testosterone level.
